{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>In all the world</b> — like <i>qav leqav</i> (line upon line), and it is the writing, and the mem of <i>qom</i> returns to the heavens. The meaning: for their writing is read in every place, and all the discerning in all places of the earth will understand my meaning." "<b>And at the end of the world</b> — it is the inhabited earth. From them they send forth voice, and behold a telling; and the <i>qav</i> (line) is the <i>sefer</i> (book/writing), and they are what the author of Sefer Yetzirah mentioned in <i>sefer</i> and <i>sefer</i> and <i>sippur</i> (narration), for these three are the roots of all wisdoms." "<b>The reason to mention the sun</b> is that it is greater than every body, and all the upper motions are bound to it, and it generates equal time and unequal, day and night, and the metals and the plants and all living things depend on the sun. Thus Solomon said <i>tachat ha-shemesh</i> (under the sun). <b>And like a bridegroom</b> — like <i>ish le-oholav</i> (each man to his tent), for the sun is fixed in the sphere with complete proofs from the wisdom of the craft of the heavens. Some say: <i>ke-demut or</i> — and like it <i>lo ye-ahil</i>. In my opinion: the alef of <i>ye-ahil</i> is added, like the alef of <i>ve-ha'aznikhah</i> naharot, and it is from the root <i>lo yehelu oram</i>. <b>In them</b> — in the heavens, and it [= the sun] is hidden from the eyes of earth's dwellers, corresponding to the distance of the lands from the far east; and they likened it to a bridegroom because all who see it rejoice in it." "<b>The meaning of 'like a mighty one'</b> — because its sphere courses with it [= through it], and it neither wearies nor tires."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "Text of <i>ve-ha'aznikhah</i> translated hyper-literally; it is obscure and possibly corrupt. <i>Ke-demut or</i> and the subsequent <i>lo ye-ahil</i> appear to be an alternate reading tradition cited by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:57.423168761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}